[HYP-C3] theta-form depression by relation SUPPORT (float; Tmax=6):
   sum of nonzero-relation terms, grouped by |support|. Negative sum = depression.
   {1,2,3}: floor(6/7)^k=0.62974
       support 2: sum of terms = +0.10462
       support 3: sum of terms = -0.03635
     theta-approx L (Tmax=6) = 0.69801   exact L = 0.69048
     => largest depression from support 3 (-0.03635)
   {1,2,3,4,5}: floor(6/7)^k=0.46266
       support 2: sum of terms = +0.16507
       support 3: sum of terms = -0.18018
       support 4: sum of terms = +0.09059
     theta-approx L (Tmax=6) = 0.53815   exact L = 0.50476
     => largest depression from support 3 (-0.18018)

[HYP-C2] TIGHT-LOCUS <-> RESONANCE-ATLAS equivalence sketch:
   tight (L=0) configs found in canon: AP{1..13}, sporadic {1..11,13,24}, Goddyn-Wong T5.
   Each is a SATURATING small-denominator relation pattern (AP: t=(1,-2,1,..) support-3 chains).
   The L7 resonance atlas = small-denom ratios p/q in (1,2.15). CLAIM: tight-locus
   finiteness <=> these saturating relation patterns are finitely many. Both reduce to
   'small-denominator commensurability is bounded'. Tested structurally, not proved.
